## Explanation

I have demonstrated mastery of server-side programming principles across multiple languages (Python, Go, and PHP) and web architectures:

### 1. Python & FastAPI (UA Arcade Cabinet)
For the UA Arcade Cabinet project, I developed an API that serves HTML5 game packages and handles dynamic asset replacement on-the-fly. The backend is built with FastAPI. In [game.py](https://github.com/Thomas-More-Digital-Innovation/2526-UAnt-007-Arcade-cabinet/blob/main/code/backend/src/game/game.py), the `serve_game_file` route intercepts game asset requests, checks if a custom override exists in the database, and dynamically streams the custom asset using FastAPI's `StreamingResponse` instead of the original resource.

### 2. Go & Bun ORM (JC Backend WASM)
For the JC Backend WASM project, I implemented a REST API in Go using the Gin web framework and Bun ORM to connect to a PostgreSQL database. In [main.go](https://github.com/Thomas-More-Digital-Innovation/2526-JC-002-Backend-WASM/blob/main/code/api/main.go), I structured the database connection lifecycle, ran migrations automatically on startup, parsed incoming JSON payloads, and executed database transactions (such as upserting statuses and creating new Todo records).

### 3. PHP & Laravel (Employment Interest Tool)
For the Employment Interest Tool, I implemented the server-side test resuming logic. In [Test.php](https://github.com/Thomas-More-Digital-Innovation/2526-MPI-001-Employment-Interest-Tool/blob/main/code/app/Livewire/Test/Test.php), the component checks if an active test attempt exists in the session. If so, it query-joins the answers and questions tables to find the last answered question and automatically resumes from the next question:

```php
// Find the last answered question to resume from the next one
$lastAnswer = Answer::join('question', 'answer.question_id', '=', 'question.question_id')
    ->where('answer.test_attempt_id', $this->testAttemptId)
    ->orderBy('question.question_number', 'desc')
    ->first();
if ($lastAnswer) {
    // Resume from the next question after the last answered one
    $this->questionNumber = $lastAnswer->question_number + 1;
    
    // If we've answered all questions, go to the last one
    if ($this->questionNumber > $this->totalQuestions) {
        $this->questionNumber = $this->totalQuestions;
    }
} else {
    // No answers yet, start from question 1
    $this->questionNumber = 1;
}
```

